{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RTdCMQYiW5AsZ4XRaTQaVU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though specific 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form details were not fully available in the results. Here's what I found:\n\n## Key Information About CoRL 2026\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US, and OpenReview serves as the platform for CoRL 2026 Conference.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and must have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics conference (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## Review Process\n\nThe accepted papers and reviews will be publicly accessible and de-anonymized after decisions are announced, with at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n**Note:** The search results did not include specific details about the 2026 reviewer guidelines document or the exact review form. For the most current and detailed reviewer guidelines and review form for CoRL 2026, I recommend checking the OpenReview page directly at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference or contacting the CoRL organizers through their official website at www.corl.org.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b41b243d-0e5c-47b1-83bb-7de38ac1f796","uuid":"560b9780-944d-49da-acb5-56775819975e","timestamp":"2026-05-15T23:04:46.928Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01RPaHP8qhH3RPhmstfkFDwN","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though specific 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form details were not fully available in the results. Here's what I found:\n\n## Key Information About CoRL 2026\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US, and OpenReview serves as the platform for CoRL 2026 Conference.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and must have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics conference (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## Review Process\n\nThe accepted papers and reviews will be publicly accessible and de-anonymized after decisions are announced, with at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n**Note:** The search results did not include specific details about the 2026 reviewer guidelines document or the exact review form. For the most current and detailed reviewer guidelines and review form for CoRL 2026, I recommend checking the OpenReview page directly at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference or contacting the CoRL organizers through their official website at www.corl.org."],"durationSeconds":5.83515785}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UPE2oABdYSdzNJkmSj7SfP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information related to CoRL conference reviewer guidelines, though the specific information for CoRL 2025 is limited. Here's what I found:\n\n**From CoRL 2024 (most recent available details):**\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nPapers can be desk rejected for formatting issues (if too long or in incorrect format), anonymity violation (if the manuscript or links identify authors), or scope issues.\n\nAll CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning either by explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or by testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\n**General CoRL Reviewer Guidelines:**\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly while pointing out obvious shortcomings not reported by authors and reflecting these in scores. Reviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, suggest improvements, and make reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\nThe search results show information from CoRL 2023 and 2024, but the specific detailed scoring rubric and review form for CoRL 2025 don't appear to be publicly available yet in these search results. You may want to check the official CoRL 2025 OpenReview page directly for the most current reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b41b243d-0e5c-47b1-83bb-7de38ac1f796","uuid":"f7e02eea-825e-4a46-8169-68e31f936b26","timestamp":"2026-05-15T23:04:47.552Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01RS3zGoZvpMen91b2CMbJjJ","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 20