{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KZYH4VasV4AirecYdSkfXq","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2023 Review Form Analysis\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, I cannot extract a complete numerical scoring rubric with specific scale points and labels. The document does not contain the actual review form itself—only guidelines for reviewers.\n\n## Available Review Dimensions\n\nThe guidelines specify six evaluation criteria:\n\n1. **Originality** — \"Are the problems or methods new?\" addressing novelty and differentiation from prior work\n2. **Quality** — \"Is the submission technically sound?\" including methodological rigor and honesty about strengths/weaknesses\n3. **Clarity** — \"Is the submission clearly written?\" addressing organization and reproducibility\n4. **Significance** — \"Are the results important?\" assessing impact and state-of-the-art advancement\n5. **Relevance** — \"Does the paper address a problem in robot learning?\" specific to CoRL's scope\n6. **Limitations** — Assessment of how authors handle shortcomings versus unreported flaws\n\n## Missing Information\n\nThe actual numerical scales (e.g., 1-5, 1-10), overall recommendation options (accept/reject/borderline), and confidence scores are **not included** in this guidelines document. These would appear in the OpenReview submission system itself, which isn't reproduced here."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b41b243d-0e5c-47b1-83bb-7de38ac1f796","uuid":"f8c33095-40df-4658-9e5c-8b6ea5d86a1d","timestamp":"2026-05-15T23:05:20.123Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":105095,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2023 Review Form Analysis\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, I cannot extract a complete numerical scoring rubric with specific scale points and labels. The document does not contain the actual review form itself—only guidelines for reviewers.\n\n## Available Review Dimensions\n\nThe guidelines specify six evaluation criteria:\n\n1. **Originality** — \"Are the problems or methods new?\" addressing novelty and differentiation from prior work\n2. **Quality** — \"Is the submission technically sound?\" including methodological rigor and honesty about strengths/weaknesses\n3. **Clarity** — \"Is the submission clearly written?\" addressing organization and reproducibility\n4. **Significance** — \"Are the results important?\" assessing impact and state-of-the-art advancement\n5. **Relevance** — \"Does the paper address a problem in robot learning?\" specific to CoRL's scope\n6. **Limitations** — Assessment of how authors handle shortcomings versus unreported flaws\n\n## Missing Information\n\nThe actual numerical scales (e.g., 1-5, 1-10), overall recommendation options (accept/reject/borderline), and confidence scores are **not included** in this guidelines document. These would appear in the OpenReview submission system itself, which isn't reproduced here.","durationMs":4915,"url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}}
