{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WcpV55QxUXsocbabgk5pyH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LRyiVwgFhrS7Qia3FaH8E2","name":"Glob","input":{"pattern":"**/*.pdf","path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3014,"cache_read_input_tokens":32442,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3014,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EFrS9JYr5QQdkwMT9ueEb4","session_id":"b41b243d-0e5c-47b1-83bb-7de38ac1f796","uuid":"80094bee-998d-43c8-a678-d905611315fd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Cy6gDzEJy8jbddTUNcc6fE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SdJbmCq6CS5RgPBX3pjaZX","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus is **Novelty and Related Work**. Write an independent, detailed review.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\"The LLM as a Redundant Bottleneck: Representational Analysis of Action Structure in Vision-Language-Action Models\"\n\nThis paper performs RSA and CKA representational analysis on an OpenVLA-class VLA (SigLIP vision encoder + projector + 32-layer LLM) across three LIBERO benchmarks. Key findings:\n1. Vision-language pretraining dominance: SigLIP+projector RSA ρ=0.615 > full VLA ρ≈0.488. CLIP-ViT (ρ=0.56) attributes 76% of SigLIP-DINO gap to VL pretraining.\n2. LLM as redundant bottleneck: Per-layer RSA U-shape (0.59→0.38→0.55), recovery ratio 85%, Spearman monotonicity -0.18.\n3. Instruction content not utilized but noise harmful: real vs no-inst Δ=0.004, random inst Δ=0.043.\n4. Metric dependency: CKA SigLIP-VLA gap = 0.02 vs RSA gap = 0.127.\n5. Cross-benchmark replication on LIBERO-Goal, Long, Spatial.\n\n## Related Work in Paper (Section 2, ~3 paragraphs)\n- VLA Models: RT-2 [Brohan 2023], OpenVLA [Kim 2024]\n- Behavioral Evidence: Grant et al. (2026), Hou et al. (2026; LangGap), Fei et al. (2025; LIBERO-Plus)\n- Representational Analysis: RSA [Kriegeskorte 2008], CKA [Kornblith 2019], Fang et al. (2025)\n- Total references: 10\n\n## Review Dimensions\nFocus your review on:\n\n### Novelty Assessment\n- Is this the first component-level representational decomposition of VLAs? (claimed as such)\n- The \"redundant bottleneck\" framing: how novel is this conceptual contribution?\n- RSA and CKA are standard tools from neuroscience/representation learning — the novelty is in the application domain\n- Prior work (Grant 2026, Hou 2026, Fei 2025) already established behavioral-level evidence for visual dominance and instruction insensitivity. How much does representational analysis add?\n- The metric dependency finding (CKA vs RSA disagreement) — is this a methodological contribution?\n\n### Related Work Gaps\n- Missing VLA architectures beyond RT-2/OpenVLA: Octo [Team et al. 2024], π0 [Black et al. 2024], GR-1 [Wu et al. 2024], RoboFlamingo [Li et al. 2023], etc.\n- Missing representation learning for robotics: R3M [Nair et al. 2022], VIP [Ma et al. 2023], MVP [Radosavovic et al. 2023], Voltron [Karamcheti et al. 2023]\n- Missing analysis of LLMs as planners/reasoners: SayCan [Ahn et al. 2022], Inner Monologue [Huang et al. 2023], Code as Policies [Liang et al. 2023]\n- Missing probing/interpretability in LLMs: extensive literature on probing classifiers, representation engineering\n- No discussion of when LLM IS useful (multi-step reasoning, compositional generalization, novel task specification)\n\n### Significance for CoRL\n- CoRL values robot learning contributions with practical impact\n- This is a pure analysis paper with no architectural improvements demonstrated\n- All experiments are in LIBERO simulation\n- The \"architectural implications\" (simplify VLA) are speculative without proof-of-concept\n- Does this advance the state of robot learning, or is it primarily a negative/diagnostic result?\n\nWrite your review in this format:\n1. Summary (2-3 sentences)\n2. Strengths (bulleted)\n3. Weaknesses (bulleted, numbered W1-W6+)\n4. Questions for Authors (numbered Q1-Q5+)\n5. Minor Issues\n6. Scores: Soundness (1-4), Presentation (1-4), Contribution (1-4), Overall (1-10), Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. CoRL acceptance rate ~28%."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":808,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1014,"cache_read_input_tokens":58769,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1014},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b41b243d-0e5c-47b1-83bb-7de38ac1f796","uuid":"b4d6a47d-3bd4-40c8-ab0f-0459302ebdf9"}
